From fbe46debc3bcd246cd6aceebc91dbd6cfe38f3a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:23:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] httpd/webui: v1.3.2 - fix Traffic Analyzer endpoint serving
 live.json for every window (renderHist crash on non-array wan)

Symptom: all history windows blank + the QoS-off class message never showed.
Console: 'wan.map is not a function' in renderHist. m5.json was fine (valid,
real data); the CGI was serving live.json for EVERY window request.

Cause: do_reaper_traffic_cgi read the window via strstr(url, "f="), but httpd
(httpd.c ~1493) strips the query string from url before the output handler
runs, so f= was never found and want fell through to the 'live' default.
renderHist then received a live payload whose wan is an object {rx_bps,tx_bps},
and .map() threw before drawing anything (which also suppressed the QoS-off
gate message that draws later in the same function).

Fix:
- web.c do_reaper_traffic_cgi: read the window with get_cgi("f") - the paired
  do_html_post_and_get input handler parses the query into the cgi table before
  this output handler runs. Still matched against the fixed 5-literal allowlist
  so the served path is never request-controlled.
- www/Reaper_Traffic.asp renderHist: treat a non-array wan as empty
  (Array.isArray guard) so a mismatched/bad payload can never throw and blank
  the whole page again.

Collector itself was already confirmed working on metal (live.json top-talkers
showed real per-client up/down bytes). EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.3.2. Metal test:
the 24h/14d/etc. windows draw WAN + per-class + per-network + top-devices from
history; QoS-off shows the class gate message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf               |  2 +-
 release/src/router/httpd/web.c            | 14 +++++++++-----
 release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp |  4 +++-
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 53a8015d6e..272d2f9cc6 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.3.1
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.3.2
 
 RCNO=0
diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
index 5578c3883d..f9dc718cf4 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/web.c
@@ -21655,16 +21655,20 @@ do_reaper_traffic_cgi(char *url, FILE *stream)
 	static const char *wins[] = { "live", "m5", "hour", "day", "month", NULL };
 	char path[48], buf[4096];
 	const char *want = "live";
-	char *q;
+	char *fp;
 	FILE *f;
 	size_t n;
 	int i;
 
-	if ((q = strstr(url, "f=")) != NULL) {
+	/* the query string is stripped from `url` before this output handler runs
+	 * (httpd.c splits at '?'), but the paired do_html_post_and_get input handler
+	 * already parsed it into the cgi table - read the window name from there.
+	 * Matched against the fixed allowlist so the served path is one of five
+	 * literals, never request-controlled. */
+	fp = get_cgi("f");
+	if (fp) {
 		for (i = 0; wins[i]; i++) {
-			size_t l = strlen(wins[i]);
-			if (strncmp(q + 2, wins[i], l) == 0 &&
-			    (q[2 + l] == '\0' || q[2 + l] == '&')) {
+			if (strcmp(fp, wins[i]) == 0) {
 				want = wins[i];
 				break;
 			}
diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp
index 90817df1c2..197df576c3 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Reaper_Traffic.asp
@@ -361,7 +361,9 @@ function renderLive(d){
 
 /* ---- render history window ---- */
 function renderHist(d){
-  var wan=d.wan||[], rx=wan.map(function(p){return p[0];}), tx=wan.map(function(p){return p[1];});
+  /* defensive: a history payload always has an array wan; never let a bad/
+     mismatched response (e.g. a live payload) throw and blank the whole page */
+  var wan=Array.isArray(d.wan)?d.wan:[], rx=wan.map(function(p){return p[0];}), tx=wan.map(function(p){return p[1];});
   var step=d.step||300, div=step>0?step:2592000;
   var rxbps=rx.map(function(v){return v*8/div;}), txbps=tx.map(function(v){return v*8/div;});
   var maxv=Math.max(1,Math.max.apply(null,rxbps),Math.max.apply(null,txbps));
-- 
2.25.1

